WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.408
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:09.315
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.984
Unit sixteen: Future Plans. Today you will talk about your plans and goals for the future.

4
00:00:15.284 --> 00:00:17.762
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:22.130
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:23.973
Ambition.

7
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.923
Ambition means a strong wish to achieve something.

8
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:30.516
My ambition is to be an architect.

9
00:00:31.117 --> 00:00:33.839
Your turn. Say: Ambition.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.666
Ambition.

11
00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:39.569
Aspire.

12
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:43.512
Aspire means to hope strongly to achieve something.

13
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:45.884
I aspire to study abroad.

14
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:49.194
Your turn. Say: Aspire.

15
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.162
Aspire.

16
00:00:53.917 --> 00:00:55.127
Career path.

17
00:00:56.117 --> 00:00:59.730
Career path means the jobs you do as you develop your work life.

18
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:02.641
Engineering is a good career path.

19
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.483
Your turn. Say: Career path.

20
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:10.601
Career path.

21
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.328
Dream job.

22
00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:15.514
Dream job means the job you want most.

23
00:01:16.117 --> 00:01:18.174
My dream job is a game designer.

24
00:01:18.783 --> 00:01:21.378
Your turn. Say: Dream job.

25
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:25.525
Dream job.

26
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:27.342
Achieve.

27
00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.685
Achieve means to succeed in doing something after hard work.

28
00:01:32.283 --> 00:01:33.935
You can achieve your goals.

29
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.144
Your turn. Say: Achieve.

30
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.989
Achieve.

31
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:42.716
Determined.

32
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:46.564
Determined means not stopping until you succeed.

33
00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.708
She is determined to win.

34
00:01:49.317 --> 00:01:51.818
Your turn. Say: Determined.

35
00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:55.563
Determined.

36
00:01:56.317 --> 00:01:57.817
Long-term goal.

37
00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:03.266
Long-term goal means something you want to achieve in many years.

38
00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.221
My long-term goal is to be a doctor.

39
00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:10.212
Your turn. Say: Long-term goal.

40
00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.474
Long-term goal.

41
00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:16.229
Motivation.

42
00:02:17.217 --> 00:02:20.981
Motivation means the reason or energy that makes you want to do something.

43
00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:23.548
My family is my motivation.

44
00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:26.930
Your turn. Say: Motivation.

45
00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:30.745
Motivation.

46
00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:32.148
Aim.

47
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.881
Aim means to plan or try to achieve something.

48
00:02:36.483 --> 00:02:38.158
I aim to get an A in English.

49
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.333
Your turn. Say: Aim.

50
00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:44.901
Aim.

51
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:46.500
Pursue.

52
00:02:47.517 --> 00:02:50.573
Pursue means to work hard to get or do something over time.

53
00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:52.846
He wants to pursue music.

54
00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:55.963
Your turn. Say: Pursue.

55
00:02:58.800 --> 00:02:59.836
Pursue.

56
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:01.457
Vision.

57
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.332
Vision means a clear idea of the future you want.

58
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:08.090
I have a vision of a cleaner Cambodia.

59
00:03:08.683 --> 00:03:11.278
Your turn. Say: Vision.

60
00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:15.053
Vision.

61
00:03:15.817 --> 00:03:16.887
Potential.

62
00:03:17.883 --> 00:03:20.916
Potential means abilities that can develop in the future.

63
00:03:21.517 --> 00:03:23.505
Every student has great potential.

64
00:03:24.117 --> 00:03:26.409
Your turn. Say: Potential.

65
00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:30.245
Potential.

66
00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:35.044
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:35.883 --> 00:03:38.417
Visal, what are you going to do after high school?

68
00:03:39.517 --> 00:03:42.828
I'm going to study architecture at university.

69
00:03:43.917 --> 00:03:46.325
That's a great ambition! Why?

70
00:03:47.417 --> 00:03:51.741
I have a vision. I'm going to design green buildings in Phnom Penh.

71
00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.397
How are you going to achieve it?

72
00:03:55.483 --> 00:03:59.213
I'm going to study hard and practise drawing every day.

73
00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.018
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:02.883 --> 00:04:05.730
Grammar focus: going to for future plans.

75
00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.206
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:09.475
I am going to study hard.

77
00:04:10.383 --> 00:04:12.278
I am going to pursue design.

78
00:04:13.183 --> 00:04:15.078
She is going to become a nurse.

79
00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.880
Use 'going to' for plans you have already decided.

80
00:04:19.617 --> 00:04:23.128
Be careful! Don't say: I going to study design.

81
00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:27.252
Say: I am going to study design.

82
00:04:27.552 --> 00:04:30.062
Don't forget am, is or are before 'going to'.

83
00:04:30.867 --> 00:04:33.728
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:34.533 --> 00:04:36.324
My Vision for the Future.

85
00:04:36.624 --> 00:04:39.274
My ambition is to pursue a career in design.

86
00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:43.334
I'm going to study art and technology at university.

87
00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:48.109
My long-term goal is to design beautiful, eco-friendly homes.

88
00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:53.038
My family is my motivation, and I'm determined to achieve my dream.

89
00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:57.693
I believe every young person has the potential to change the future.

90
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:02.616
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.275
I blank going to study medicine.

92
00:05:05.575 --> 00:05:08.730
A, am. B, is. C, are.

93
00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:13.825
The answer is A: am.

94
00:05:14.983 --> 00:05:17.424
Not stopping until you succeed is blank.

95
00:05:17.724 --> 00:05:21.668
A, determined. B, potential. C, vision.

96
00:05:25.233 --> 00:05:27.268
The answer is A: determined.

97
00:05:28.417 --> 00:05:31.194
The reason that makes you want to do something is blank.

98
00:05:31.494 --> 00:05:35.008
A, motivation. B, ambition. C, career.

99
00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.613
The answer is A: motivation.

100
00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.952
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:45.817 --> 00:05:48.710
What is one goal you aspire to achieve in the future?

102
00:05:57.517 --> 00:05:59.110
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:07.728
I aspire to become a software engineer. I'm going to study computer science, and I'm going to build apps for Cambodian students.

104
00:06:08.028 --> 00:06:09.807
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:10.717 --> 00:06:15.227
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and going to for future plans.

106
00:06:15.527 --> 00:06:19.642
Today's value is ambition. Dream big and work hard for your future.

107
00:06:19.942 --> 00:06:22.780
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.731
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

